{"id":"a9","level":2,"levelName":"Ulpan Alef","n":14,"of":16,"title":"What's happening now","titleHe":"זְמַן הֹוֶה","goal":"Use the present tense — four forms, no persons.","sections":[{"type":"text","body":"The Hebrew present has only four forms, and they change for gender and number rather than for person. אֲנִי כּוֹתֵב, אַתָּה כּוֹתֵב and הוּא כּוֹתֵב are all the same word — the pronoun does the rest."},{"type":"binyan","he":"פָּעַל","en":"pa'al (kal)","note":"The plain, basic verb — the one most everyday actions use.","verb":{"root":"כ־ת־ב","inf":"לִכְתֹּב","en":"to write"},"tense":"present","rows":[{"label":"masculine singular","he":"","form":"כּוֹתֵב"},{"label":"feminine singular","he":"","form":"כּוֹתֶבֶת"},{"label":"masculine plural","he":"","form":"כּוֹתְבִים"},{"label":"feminine plural","he":"","form":"כּוֹתְבוֹת"}]},{"type":"text","body":"It covers both English presents at once: אֲנִי קוֹרֵא is I read and I am reading."},{"type":"examples","items":[{"he":"אֲנִי לוֹמֵד עִבְרִית.","en":"I'm learning Hebrew."},{"he":"הִיא גָּרָה בָּעִיר.","en":"She lives in the city."},{"he":"הֵם אוֹכְלִים בַּבַּיִת.","en":"They're eating at home."}]}],"vocab":[{"he":"לוֹמֵד","en":"learns, studies","translit":"lomed"},{"he":"כּוֹתֵב","en":"writes","translit":"kotev"},{"he":"קוֹרֵא","en":"reads","translit":"kore"},{"he":"אוֹכֵל","en":"eats","translit":"ochel"},{"he":"הוֹלֵךְ","en":"goes, walks","translit":"holech"},{"he":"יוֹשֵׁב","en":"sits","translit":"yoshev"},{"he":"גָּר","en":"lives, resides","translit":"gar"},{"he":"רוֹצֶה","en":"wants","translit":"rotse"},{"he":"אוֹהֵב","en":"loves, likes","translit":"ohev"},{"he":"עִבְרִית","en":"Hebrew","translit":"ivrit"}],"exercises":[{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["learns, studies","place","fox","in the end"],"correct":0,"prompt":"לוֹמֵד","translit":"lomed"},{"type":"choice","q":"What does this mean?","options":["a lot, many","therefore","writes","healthy"],"correct":2,"prompt":"כּוֹתֵב","translit":"kotev"}